From 52587b6f5dde95937fbec43a76a25d161214b764 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Klemm <github@tklemm.eu>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:35:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Build attribute Hashes without copying the lazy row

LazyIndexedAttributeSet#attributes copies the set's attributes into a new
IndexedRow::Mutable on every call. AttributeSet#values_for_database and
#values_before_type_cast, which back attributes_for_database (used by
Marshal and the MessagePack coder) and attributes_before_type_cast, only
turn that row into a Hash.

They now read the attributes materialize built straight from the set, by
name in the order of its indexes, as IndexedRow#transform_values does.
They build the same attributes and call the same method on each, so the
Hashes and the record's state afterwards are unchanged.

Reading values from the row instead, as #to_hash does, would also skip
materialize, but wouldn't be the same: Attribute#value_for_database keeps
the value it returns, so an encrypted attribute dumps the same ciphertext
each time, and accessed_fields would leave out attributes read as nil.
---
 activemodel/lib/active_model/attribute_set.rb | 24 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/activemodel/lib/active_model/attribute_set.rb b/activemodel/lib/active_model/attribute_set.rb
index 84784dc584..e6bffa3b7a 100644
--- a/activemodel/lib/active_model/attribute_set.rb
+++ b/activemodel/lib/active_model/attribute_set.rb
@@ -370,6 +370,30 @@ def to_hash
     end
     alias :to_h :to_hash
 
+    #: () -> Hash[String, untyped]
+    def values_before_type_cast
+      materialize
+      hash = {}
+      indexes.each_key do |name|
+        if attribute = lookup(index_for_name(name))
+          hash[name] = attribute.value_before_type_cast
+        end
+      end
+      hash
+    end
+
+    #: () -> Hash[String, untyped]
+    def values_for_database
+      materialize
+      hash = {}
+      indexes.each_key do |name|
+        if attribute = lookup(index_for_name(name))
+          hash[name] = attribute.value_for_database
+        end
+      end
+      hash
+    end
+
     #: (String) ?{ (String) -> untyped } -> untyped
     def fetch_value(name, &block)
       index = index_for_name(name)
